    <h1>Dog Food Allergies & Novel Proteins</h1>
    <p class="lead text-xl">If your dog is constantly itching or has chronic gastrointestinal issues, they might have a food allergy.</p>
    <h2>What causes food allergies?</h2>
    <p>Most dogs are allergic to common proteins like chicken, beef, or dairy. When trying to diagnose an allergy, a veterinarian will usually recommend a novel protein diet.</p>
    <h2>What is a novel protein?</h2>
    <p>A novel protein is simply a meat source your dog has never eaten before. If they've never eaten kangaroo, they can't be allergic to it. We offer kangaroo, venison, and alligator single-ingredient treats for exactly this reason.</p>
